{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c40f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa23-73f9-7152-a6b5-3fcdf5d3c2f1"},"sequence":98,"recorded_at":1780531400000191,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","event":{"chunk":"Read text file `PLAN.md`.\n(497 line(s) above)\n498|### Screens\n499|\n500|- **Dialogue box:** bottom strip, white; speaker name in teal; typewriter at about 40 cps, in sync with voice syllables; ✕ completes, then advances; hold to skip fast. Ounce gets a small dial portrait with a mood needle.\n501|- **Results, station menu, Hall of Numbers, Locker Room, Sweat Jar, Report:** one focal element each, big numbers, 1-2 lines of comment.\n502|- **Locker Room:** on a turntable; skin (sand, orange, red, plum), hair style and colour, top, bottom, headband, jar unlocks.\n503|- **Name entry:** letter grid (stick, d-pad, click) plus direct typing, 8 characters max.\n504|\n505|### Pause menu\n506|\n507|`engine.timeScale = 0` ✔ freezes physics, `fixedUpdate` and game time while `update` still runs and `wasPressed` still works. Menus therefore read input in `update`. Don't use `engine.paused` for this.\n508|\n509|Resume / Restart activity / Back to the island / Settings / How to play / About & Credits / **Dev Tools**. In a session: Resume and Settings only, and nothing freezes.\n510|\n511|### Settings (own HUD menu, not the engine panel)\n512|\n513|Music volume (**default 10%**), SFX, Voice, Button glyphs (PlayStation / Xbox), Gentle Mode (rings ×1.25, noise ×.8), Mouse lean radius, Step timing offset, Reduce flashes, Look (Default, `storybook`, `arcade`, `handheld`), Pixel size (`engine.settings.set({ look, pixelSize })`), Fullscreen, Reset to defaults.\n514|\n515|### Touch-only devices\n516|\n517|Detect ✔ `matchMedia('(hover: none) and (pointer: coarse)')` with no gamepad. Start with `touch: false` always, and `settings: { button: 'top-right' }` only on such devices (otherwise `button: false`). ✔ The ⚙ appears and a tap opens the engine's panel. Show over the title: **\"Controller or keyboard required\"**, wrapped: a portrait phone's art is as narrow as 168 px wide. Attract runs and loops. A tap returns to the title message and the 10 s timer restarts. If a pad connects or a key is pressed, drop the message and play normally.\n518|\n519|---\n520|\n521|## 10. Dev mode\n522|\n523|Reached from the pause menu, not in sessions. 10-foot legible and fully controller-driven. Tabs with L1/R1.\n524|\n525|**Sliders (live, each read by the code every step; registry in `src/core/tunables.js`):**\n526|\n527|| Tab | Variables, with defaults |\n528||---|---|\n529|| Balance | dotInstability .6, dotAuthority 3, dotDamping 3.4, dotNoise .8, dotLag .08, ringScale 1, gustForce 1.6, mouseLeanRadius 70 |\n530|| Breath and reps | breathBonus .55, repLag .10, repFatigue .10, repTempoScale 1 |\n531|| Rhythm | stepWindow 1, stepOffsetMs 0, hoopLow .9, hoopHigh 2.4, hoopLiftRate .35 |\n532|| Games | headerInterval 1.0, slackWalkInst 2.6, trayGravity 9.8, trayMaxTilt 14, jogTargetCadence 3, pierBoost 2.14 |\n533|| Economy | dripRate 1, starThresholdScale 1, ageTrainingWeight .5 |\n534|\n535|Each slider shows its value and default. **One button resets the tab, one resets everything.** Export prints the changed values as JSON to the console and copies them if allowed, so a designer can paste them into `src/data/`.\n536|\n537|**Tools tab:** go to day 1-7; jump to any activity or scene; finish the current activity with 0-3★; give 50 Drips; unlock all; autopilot (bot skill picker); god mode (Dot can't leave the ring); time scale .25-3; overlay (scene, state, Dot, ring, fps, last device); hide HUD; free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset: 'free' }, { syncUrl: false })`); dialogue tester (any line, with voice); sound test (every song, SFX, speaker); animation viewer (every clip on an avatar); reset save.\n538|\n539|---\n540|\n541|## 11. Attract mode\n542|\n543|After **10 seconds with no input on the title or any menu screen**, start a looping demo:\n544|\n545|- **Playlist:** Hub walk → Holding Still → Hoop → Header → Step → Slackline → Tray → Pier Jump → Jog → Long Stand excerpt, about 14 s each, with iris transitions. Cover every activity and feature family.\n546|- It runs the **real scenes** with expert bot drivers and cheats (ring ×2, god mode). Banner: {TITLE}, \"Press any button.\" plus Ounce's subtitles (\"This is a recording...\").\n547|- **Any input exits**: key, click, mouse move past a few pixels, wheel, pad button or stick, touch. You return to the title and the timer re-arms.\n548|- Not in a session, not during play, not on the pause menu.\n549|\n550|---\n551|\n552|## 12. Multiplayer\n553|\n554|**Reading of the brief:** the hub protocol is how the game plays online; on its own the game has no server, so it plays alone or on one screen. Both run the same round, **The Medley**, and the same lane code. Nothing else connects to a network.\n555|\n556|### The Medley\n557|\n558|Three events in fixed windows: Stillness (a pose), then Beat (Reps or Hoop or Step), then Balance-lean (Header), each 55 s with 10 s between, about 3.2 minutes. The specific picks and shortened durations live in `src/data/medley.js`, and the picks come from a seeded stream. Each event normalises to 0-1000; the total wins. Results show medals, awards (\"Stillest\", \"Most Apologetic\") and Ounce's remarks.\n559|\n560|### On its own: Family Hour\n561|\n562|Join screen: **each device claims a mat by pressing Cross/Enter** (up to 4 pads plus keyboard-and-mouse). Bots can fill empty mats (toggle).\n563|\n564|**The engine merges all pads into one** ✔, so lanes read `navigator.getGamepads()` by index themselves (`applyDeadzone` is exported; guard for Node). In 4-mat staging, each player gets a small dial (radius 24) above their avatar's head. Podium, rematch.\n565|\n566|### In AI Hub: ghost mode\n567|\n568|Passed 16/16 with the real engine on WebGPU ✔ at players=1, 2, 4 (latency, jitter, loss) and host-leave.\n569|\n570|```html\n571|<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n572|<script>/* session.js pasted unmodified: first script, right after charset */</script>\n573|<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n574|<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n575|<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n576|<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most across three events. Stay in the circle.\">\n577|<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J: step.\">\n578|<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n579|<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n580|```\n581|\n582|Boot order ✔:\n583|\n584|```js\n585|let info = null;\n586|if (window.AIHub?.active) info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n587|const engine = await Engine.start(firstScene, withUrlOptions({ /* ... */ seed: info ? info.seed : savedOrDefaultSeed }));\n588|if (info) AIHub.ready();                 // no key press, as soon as the card can show\n589|```\n590|\n591|If `connect()` answers null, carry on as the normal game. Without WebGPU, `Engine.start` rejects and the engine prints \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: ...\" on the page ✔. Catch the rejection, or it also surfaces as a page error ✔, and call `AIHub.fail(message)` in a session.\n592|\n593|**In a session:**\n594|- **The card (`card: true`)** is the game's own: the players' avatars lining up on mats in seat colours (`#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`), {TITLE}, ready ticks, how to win, the controls for the last device, the time left from the `card` event. Enter or Cross → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; Triangle or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Use a **direct `keydown` listener for Enter** ✔ here. No menus. Cosmetic randomness only from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n595|- **Start:** on `start` show a countdown from `AIHub.time()`; play at `time() >= 0`. Event windows are read from `AIHub.time()`, so all copies stay in step.\n596|- **Same world:** gusts, pose picks and object waves come from `AIHub.rng(label)` or the seeded `ctx.random`.\n597|- **Ghosts:** a `setInterval` at 100 ms (not tied to rendering) sends `AIHub.send({ a: eventIndex, x, y, c: clipIndex, t: clipTime, s: score }, { reliable: false })` and calls `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`. Start as soon as `start` arrives, even with score 0: the harness needs both within seconds. Receivers lerp the other mats; they never simulate them, and they hide a ghost whose `a` differs from theirs.\n598|- **`leave`:** that avatar waves and walks off. The round goes on, host included.\n599|- **End:** `AIHub.result({ score, stats, awards })` once, at the end of the Medley or at once on `time-up`. On `end`: stop input, stop sound, send nothing.\n600|- **Never:** no title, attract, dev mode, saves, quit or restart; no chat or custom names; no `alert`, `window.open` or navigation. Names come from `info.players` and are drawn with `say()`.\n601|\n602|---\n603|\n604|## 13. Art direction\n605|\n606|**Base: the engine's native look**, default pixel pipeline, toon materials, 16-colour palette (`look` left unset). The scene reads clean and bright: white, mist, sky and cyan, with lime and sand for growth and warmth, orange and red as accents. Start with `quality: 'high'` (`'medium'` in sessions, where several copies may share a machine in testing).\n607|\n608|**Performance is out of scope.** Add the detail the scene wants and don't spend time on optimisation.\n609|\n610|### Avatars ✔\n611|\n612|Re-dress the kit's hero with the same rig. This is proven to look good at gameplay framing: egg heads, dot eyes, hair caps. Use `castShadow: false` plus `ContactShadow` ✔: casting on the model gave ugly self-shadow blotches. The hero's `Eyes` mesh reads as sunglasses, so hide it. Compile clips once and share them between avatars.\n613|\n614|```js\n615|function soften(mesh, kind = 'prism') { // same bounding box, softer shape\n616|  mesh.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n617|  const b = mesh.geometry.boundingBox, s = b.getSize(new Vector3()), c = b.getCenter(new Vector3());\n618|  const g = kind === 'egg' ? new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 8) : new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 8);\n619|  g.scale(s.x, s.y, s.z); g.translate(c.x, c.y, c.z); mesh.geometry = g;\n620|}\n621|export function dress(root, look) { // look: { skin, top, bottom, shoe, hair, long?, bun?, headband? } as palette names\n622|  const hide = new Set(['Moustache', 'ButtonR', 'ButtonL', 'Hat', 'Brim', 'Eyes', 'Nose']);\n623|  const SLOT = { Overalls: 'bottom', ThighR: 'bottom', ThighL: 'bottom', ShinR_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin', ShinL_Mesh: look.long ? 'bottom' : 'skin',\n624|    Shirt: 'top', SleeveR: 'top', SleeveL: 'top', ForearmR_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin', ForearmL_Mesh: look.long ? 'top' : 'skin',\n625|    GloveR: 'skin', GloveL: 'skin', Face: 'skin', ShoeR: 'shoe', ShoeL: 'shoe' };\n626|  root.traverse((o) => {\n627|    if (!o.isMesh) return;\n628|    if (hide.has(o.name)) { o.visible = false; return; }\n629|    if (SLOT[o.name]) o.material = toonMaterial(PALETTE[look[SLOT[o.name]]]);\n630|    if (o.name === 'Face') soften(o, 'egg'); else if (/Sleeve|Forearm|Thigh|Shin|Glove/.test(o.name)) soften(o);\n631|  });\n632|  const face = root.getObjectByName('Face'); face.geometry.computeBoundingBox();\n633|  const fb = face.geometry.boundingBox, size = fb.getSize(new Vector3()), c = fb.getCenter(new Vector3());\n634|  const add = (m, x, y, z) => { m.position.set(x, y, z); face.parent.add(m); return m; };\n635|  for (const sx of [-1, 1]) add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.055, 0.09, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x + sx * size.x * 0.2, c.y + 0.02, c.z + size.z * 0.48);\n636|  add(new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(0.1, 0.022, 0.03), toonMaterial(PALETTE.ink)), c.x, c.y - size.y * 0.2, c.z + size.z * 0.47);\n637|  const hair = add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.5, 10, 6, 0, Math.PI * 2, 0, Math.PI * 0.55), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.04, c.z - size.z * 0.05);\n638|  hair.scale.set(size.x * 1.08, size.y * 1.04, size.z * 1.08);\n639|  if (look.bun) add(new Mesh(new SphereGeometry(0.1, 8, 6), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.hair])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.6, c.z - size.z * 0.2);\n640|  if (look.headband) { const b2 = add(new Mesh(new CylinderGeometry(0.5, 0.5, 1, 10), toonMaterial(PALETTE[look.headband])), c.x, c.y + size.y * 0.16, c.z); b2.scale.set(size.x * 1.06, 0.06, size.z * 1.06); }\n641|}\n642|```\n643|\n644|Add more hair shapes as extra meshes on the head. Good casting: player `{ skin:'sand', top:'white', bottom:'sky', shoe:'white', hair:'ink', headband:'red' }`; Coach `{ skin:'sand', top:'cyan', bottom:'cyan', shoe:'white', hair:'mist', bun:true, long:true }`, plus a plumb bob on a string (`SpringChain`) from her wrist.\n645|\n646|### Ounce ✔ (zero problems, zero warnings on the model sheet)\n647|\n648|```js\n649|export const ounce = model({\n650|  id: 'ounce', about: 'Ounce: a mint retro bathroom scale whose round dial is its face', tags: ['character'], size: [1.1, 1.05, 1.1],\n651|  palette: { body: 'cyan', base: 'teal', tread: 'sky', face: 'white', rim: 'slate', tick: 'mist', needle: 'red', eye: 'ink' },\n652|  parts: [\n653|    { name: 'base', box: [1.04, 0.08, 1.04], at: [0, 0.04, 0], c: 'base' },\n654|    { name: 'plate', box: [0.96, 0.2, 0.96], at: [0, 0.18, 0], c: 'body' },\n655|    { mirror: [{ name: 'tread', box: [0.3, 0.03, 0.42], at: [0.22, 0.295, -0.22], c: 'tread' }], axis: 'x' },\n656|    { group: [\n657|        { name: 'neck', box: [0.5, 0.42, 0.14], at: [0, 0.21, 0], c: 'body' },\n658|        { group: [\n659|            { name: 'rim', cyl: [0.78, 0.1, 0.78], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'rim', seg: 14 },\n660|            { name: 'dial', cyl: [0.66, 0.04, 0.66], at: [0, 0.06, 0], c: 'face', seg: 14 },\n661|            ...[-60, -30, 0, 30, 60].map((a) => ({ box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.09], at: [Math.sin(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26, 0.085, -Math.cos(a * Math.PI / 180) * 0.26], rot: [0, -a, 0], c: 'tick' })),\n662|            { mirror: [{ name: 'eye', box: [0.08, 0.03, 0.11], at: [0.12, 0.09, -0.07], c: 'eye' }], axis: 'x' },\n663|            { group: [{ name: 'needleBar', box: [0.06, 0.03, 0.22], at: [0, 0, 0.1], c: 'needle' }, { name: 'hub', cyl: [0.07, 0.04, 0.07], at: [0, 0, 0], c: 'needle', seg: 8 }], name: 'needle', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.1, 0.1], rot: [0, 180, 0] },\n664|          ], name: 'face', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.5, 0.08], rot: [72, 0, 0] },\n665|      ], name: 'head', pivot: true, at: [0, 0.26, 0.2] },\n666|  ],\n667|});\n668|```\n669|\n670|Pivots stay movable: `build.object.getObjectByName('needle')` for mood, `'face'` for nods. Scale Ounce ×1.4 on the island and frame close in Weigh-In. Squash on hops.\n671|\n672|### Models to write as data (`src/art/models.js`; check each with `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`)\n673|\n674|Kettlebell Volcano ✔ (`ball [12,9,12]`, `torus` handle, glowing top), Foam Roller Hill ✔ (a big `cyl` on its side with bands), Dumbbell Bridge ✔, medicine ball ✔, Pavilion ✔ (columns, `cone` roof, recolour per station), Sweat Jar ✔ (`{ lathe: [[.85,0],[.95,.1],[.95,2.1],[.75,2.4],[.75,2.55]], at: [0,.3,0], seg: 12 }` for the glass, plus plinth, lid and label; **toon materials are opaque, so fake the fluid**: a `sky` cylinder 1 cm wider than the wall, scaled in y with Drips, with a white highlight stripe), Rep Shed, Beat Stage with speakers, pier with railings, palm (`tube` trunk, fronds; the library has none), yoga mat, step platform, hoop (`torus`), coconut, flip-flop, golden pineapple, catapult, tray and cups, vitamin, slackline anchors, hammock, lockers, Hall of Numbers board, judges' paddles, mobility scooter, ferry, water cup, sprinkler, Kevin (body, wings, feet, with a two-pose flap).\n675|\n676|From the library, generic props are fine: `fountain`, `bench`, `lamp-post`, `bush`, `flowers`, `oak`, `fence`, `signpost`, `table`.\n677|\n678|### Surfaces and scene effects\n679|\n680|- **Tile floor ✔:** `textureDef({ id:'clinic-tile', size:[16,16], tile:true, palette:{ grout:'mist', a:'white', b:'white' }, layers:[{ pattern:'tiles', colors:['grout','a','b'], w:16, h:16, mortar:1, seed:3 }], about:'...', tags:['floor'] })`, added to `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`. **Never stretch a map over a box ✔** (it gave one giant tile): use a `PlaneGeometry` and scale its UVs by metres ÷ (16 / `DEFAULT_TEXEL`), as the kit's market example does.\n681|- **World:** `WaterSurface` ✔, `GrassField` ✔, sand and lawn as flat boxes ✔, `RippleField` at splashes, `Precipitation` in the finale, `Boids` gulls, `Decals` footprints on sand.\n682|- **Light:** `ctx.lights` for pavilion lanterns at dusk; `applySky(skyAt(h))` for morning and evening.\n683|- **Game feel:** `hitstop`, `shake`, `screen.flash`, `screen.shockwave` on the splash, iris transitions (`screen.cover`/`reveal` ✔, also resolve headless), `Trail` behind the jogger, custom particles ('sweat' in cyan, 'confetti', 'splash', 'zen' motes).\n684|- **Cutscenes:** ferry arrival, confession and ending with `Timeline` ✔. On the `fixed` preset, apply `tl.camera()` each frame to `ctx.camera.camera` (position, `lookAt`, fov, `updateProjectionMatrix`) ✔. Use `tl.line()` for subtitles, `tl.bars()` for letterbox.\n685|\n686|---\n687|\n688|## 14. Animation\n689|\n690|Use the engine's native system: `ClipDef` data, `compileClips`, `THREE.AnimationMixer` for class avatars, `PlatformerCharacter` on the island, procedural layers (`Squash`, `SpringChain`) for character.\n691|\n692|**Conventions** (`HERO_RIG`): facing +Z. Arm X: -90 ahead, -180 overhead. Arm Z: out to the side (R negative, L positive). Forearm -X bends the elbow. Leg -X swings forward. Shin +X bends the knee. Foot +X points the toes. Pelvis `p` offsets, `r` tips the whole body. Torso +X bends forward.\n693|\n694|**Verified poses ✔** (`validateClip` clean, `analyzeClip` no problems, reviewed on contact sheets):\n695|\n696|```js\n697|const hold = (name, pose) => ({ name, frames: 60, loop: true, keys: [[0, pose], [60, pose]] });\n698|const feet = (pose, R, L) => placeFeet(pose, HERO_RIG, { R, L });\n699|hold('Tree', { Pelvis: { p: [0.03, -0.02, 0] }, ArmR: [-172, 0, -6], ForearmR: [-14, 0, 0], ArmL: [-172, 0, 6], ForearmL: [-14, 0, 0], LegR: [-62, 0, -58], ShinR: [150, 0, 0], FootR: [30, 0, 0] });\n700|hold('Heron', { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [10, 0, 0], Head: [-14, 0, 0], ArmR: [-20, 0, -80], ArmL: [-20, 0, 80], ForearmR: [-30, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-30, 0, 0], LegR: [-85, 0, 0], ShinR: [95, 0, 0], FootR: [35, 0, 0] });\n701|hold('Warrior', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Torso: [0, 25, 0], Head: [0, 40, 0], ArmR: [0, 0, -90], ArmL: [0, 0, 90] }, { z: 0.38 }, { z: -0.38 }));\n702|hold('Chair', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.28, -0.06] }, Torso: [24, 0, 0], Head: [-18, 0, 0], ArmR: [-110, 0, -8], ArmL: [-110, 0, 8] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\n703|hold('Fold', feet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.03, -0.03] }, Torso: [88, 0, 0], Head: [10, 0, 0], ArmR: [-70, 0, -6], ArmL: [-70, 0, 6], ForearmR: [-8, 0, 0], ForearmL: [-8, 0, 0] }, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 }));\n704|hold('Plank', { Pelvis: { r: [66, 0, 0], p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Head: [-48, 0, 0], ArmR: [-63, 0, -5], ArmL: [-63, 0, 5], HandR: [-40, 0, 0], HandL: [-40, 0, 0], FootR: [55, 0, 0], FootL: [55, 0, 0] });\n705|// Scrubbed reps: keys built with placeFeet AND a feet track, or the sole dips through the floor mid-clip.\n706|const squatTop = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.02, 0] }, Torso: [2, 0, 0], ArmR: [6, 0, -9], ArmL: [6, 0, 9] }, squatLow = { Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.3, -0.05] }, Torso: [26, 0, 0], Head: [-20, 0, 0], ArmR: [-85, 0, -8], ArmL: [-85, 0, 8] };\n707|({ name: 'SquatRep', frames: 30, grounded: true, keys: [[0, feet(squatTop, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })], [30, feet(squatLow, { z: 0 }, { z: 0 })]], feet: [[0, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }], [30, { R: { z: 0 }, L: { z: 0 } }]] });\n708|// LungeRep: the same way, low pose Pelvis p [0,-0.24,0], Torso [6,0,0], goals R { z: .34 }, L { z: -.32, pitch: 25, pivot: 'ball' }. For the left side, map poses through mirror(pose, HERO_RIG) and swap R and L goals.\n709|```\n710|\n711|**Still to author:** Press; StepL/StepR; header nod; flail; daze; bow; slow clap; sneeze; Coach's point and demonstration transitions; tuck and cannonball; judge raising a paddle; stepping onto Ounce; ferry disembark. Reuse kit clips: `Idle`, `Walk`, `Run`, `Sit`, `LieIdle`, `Wave`, `Victory`, `Teeter`, `Hurt`, `Fall`, `GetUp`, and more (`HERO_CLIPS`).\n712|\n713|**Preview without a GPU ✔:** `tools/clip-sheet.mjs` uses `renderSheet(model, HERO_RIG, def, clip, { frames, views: ['front', 'side'], scale: 90, trails: false, skeleton: false })` → `{ width, height, data }`, written as a PNG with `node:zlib` (`deflateSync`, `crc32`). Look at every new pose once. Hide the hat and moustache first so you judge the real silhouette.\n714|\n715|---\n716|\n717|## 15. Audio\n718|\n719|Everything is written in code. No audio files.\n720|\n721|### Music\n722|\n723|- **`ctx.audio.setVolume('music', savedMusic ?? 0.10)` at boot, every boot**, from your own settings key. The engine's default is 60%, and its stored volume key (`pixel-engine:audio`) is shared by every engine game on the origin, so don't rely on it.\n724|- **Write instruments loud:** track `volume` 0.45-0.8. The kit's examples use about 0.12, written for a 60% bus; at 10% × master .8 that is near silence. A test checks each song: sum of track volumes × 0.1 × 0.8 ≥ 0.03.\n725|- Songs are `Song` data, in `src/audio/songs.js`, each original, none imitating the source:\n726|\n727|| Song | Feel |\n728||---|---|\n729|| Title / Plaza | gentle waiting-room bossa, about 92 BPM, soft triangle plucks |\n730|| Holding Still | slow, sparse, breath-paced, 60 BPM |\n731|| Rep Shed | light funk bass, 110 BPM |\n732|| Beat Beach (Hoop) and Step Class | bright, four-on-the-floor; Step is 104 BPM exactly |\n733|| Lagoon Games | staccato ukulele feel, 120 BPM |\n734|| Jog | steady, cheerful, 112 BPM |\n735|| Evening Report | music box, 70 BPM |\n736|| Long Stand | near silence, then one swelling chord line at t = 75 |\n737|\n738|### SFX\n739|\n740|`ctx.audio.register` data: needle tick, ring chime in/out, wobble warning, rep tick, step perfect/good, combo, coconut bonk, flip-flop thwap, hoop whirr (`loop`), splash, gust, gull squawk, jar drip, star pop, menu move/confirm/back, \"Ow\" stinger.\n741|\n742|### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish\n743|\n744|Build in `src/audio/voice.js`:\n745|\n746|1. **`syllabify(text, speaker)` is pure and testable in Node.** Words split into syllables; a hash of each word picks consonant class and vowel, so **the same word always sounds the same**. Output: `[{ t, dur, f0, vowel, cons, charIndex }]`. Declination -15% across a sentence; `?` rises 25% at the end; `!` +15%; `...` slows. The dialogue typewriter reads `charIndex`.\n747|2. **`renderVoice(ctx, destination, syllables, when)`** schedules, per syllable: a saw oscillator at `f0` through two parallel bandpass filters at the vowel's formants (a 800/1200, e 500/1900, i 300/2300, o 500/900, u 350/800, × speaker shift), gain envelope 6 ms up, 30 ms down; a noise burst for plosives (8 ms) and fricatives (40 ms).\n748|3. **Routing:** it works on any `BaseAudioContext`, so it renders in `OfflineAudioContext` for tests. Live, use `ctx.audio.context`, connected to `ctx.audio.buses.sfx` (undocumented but present in 0.46.0, so master and mute apply) via your own Voice gain. `ctx.audio.context` is null headless and before the first input: no-op and log.\n749|\n750|| Speaker | f0 | Syllables/s | Formant shift | Extra |\n751||---|---|---|---|---|\n752|| Ounce | 340 | 13 | ×1.25 | a needle tick on punctuation |\n753|| Coach | 165 | 7.5 | ×.9 | flat pitch, long pauses |\n754|| Marguerite | 230 | 9 | ×1 | slight vibrato |\n755|| Dennis | 120 | 11 | ×.95 | pitch up on last word |\n756|| June | 300 | 10 | ×1.15 | no contour at all |\n757|| Kevin | | | | squawk SFX, never words |\n758|\n759|---\n760|\n761|## 16. Architecture\n762|\n763|Download the kit (the URL is in your brief) and copy the contents of the zip's top-level `pixel-engine/` folder into the dev folder, so `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs` and the guides sit at its root. **Never edit `pixel-engine.js`**: record its sha256 in `vendor/pixel-engine.sha256` when you unzip, and a test compares it. Fetch the hub's `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and `README.md` into `vendor/hub/` from `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/`.\n764|\n765|```\n766|pixel-engine.js  check.mjs  GUIDE.md ...        the kit, untouched\n767|vendor/hub/                                     hub client and harness, untouched\n768|src/main.js                                     boot: session check, Engine.start, first scene\n769|src/app.js                                      App: scene switching, save, settings, tunables, device, debug API\n770|src/core/      dot.js drivers.js actions.js device.js tunables.js save.js net.js clock.js\n771|src/ui/        font.js menu.js dialogue.js widgets.js prompts.js screens/*\n772|src/audio/     voice.js songs.js sfx.js\n773|src/art/       avatar.js models.js textures.js clips.js glyphs.js portraits.js\n774|src/data/      title.js activities.js poses.js reps.js charts.js boards.js week.js lines.js\n775|               questions.js unlocks.js classmates.js stations.js medley.js about.js\n776|src/scenes/    base.js boot.js title.js attract.js hub.js weighin.js report.js locker.js records.js jar.js\n777|               card.js medley.js join.js ending.js  activity/{base,poses,reps,hoop,step,header,slackline,tray,jog,pier,longstand}.js\n778|tools/         build.mjs test.mjs clip-sheet.mjs shot.mjs\n779|tests/         headless/*.mjs  browser/*.mjs\n780|```\n781|\n782|**Everything a designer would change is plain data in `src/data/`:** poses, exercises, charts, boards, schedules, lines, unlocks, stars. A new pose, chart, board or day needs no code. That is what lets the rest of the game be built out later with normal tools, together with the live sliders and their JSON export.\n783|\n784|**Engine patterns:**\n785|- Start ✔: `Engine.start(new Boot(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), aspect: 'fill', touch: false, settings: { button: touchOnly ? 'top-right' : false }, quality: info ? 'medium' : 'high', seed, background: PALETTE.sky, camera }))`.\n786|- Each scene is a `Game`, swapped with `engine.loadGame(scene, { camera })`. It frees everything per level; keep persistent state in `App`. Transition: `await screen.cover('iris')`, `await loadGame`, `await screen.reveal('iris')`.\n787|- `BaseScene` owns the frame order: `update` → `App.device.update` → overlays (pause, dialogue, dev) take input first → the scene's own update → `hud.clear()` → scene draw → overlays draw. Gameplay goes in `fixedUpdate`, skipped automatically while `timeScale` is 0.\n788|- **Rules from the guide that matter here:** gameplay in `fixedUpdate` with `consumePress`; `wasPressed` only in `update`; all randomness from `ctx.random` forks (never `Math.random`); time from `ctx.time` (never `performance.now`); no `new PointLight`. Modules guard `document`, `window`, `navigator` and `localStorage`, so **everything runs in Node** ✔.\n789|- **Drivers** (`src/core/drivers.js`): `read(out)` fills `{ x, y, breath, stepL, stepR, confirm }`. `LocalDriver` (engine input and mouse), `PadDriver(index)` (Family Hour), `BotDriver(skill)`, `GhostDriver` (display only). Attract, tests, classmates and online all reuse this one seam.\n790|- **Debug API**, kept in the shipped game (`globalThis.__GAME__ = App`): `go(id, args)`, `state()` as JSON, `setDriver(skill)`, `tunables`. Give every scene a real `status()` line (`activity hoop | play | t 31.2 | score 412`) and a `fingerprint()` (score, Dot state).\n791|\n792|---\n793|\n794|## 17. Verified recipes\n795|\n796|### Single-file build ✔ (boots on `file://` in about 1.3 s; passes `check.mjs` and the harness)\n797|\n798|```js\n799|// tools/build.mjs (esbuild is on this machine)\n800|execFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js', '--bundle', '--format=esm', '--platform=browser', '--target=esnext', '--charset=utf8', '--outfile=.build/bundle.js', '--log-level=warning'], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n801|const safe = (s) => s.replace(/<\\/script/gi, '<\\\\/script').replace(/<!--/g, '<\\\\!--');\n802|const html = `<!doctype html>\n803|<html lang=\"en\"><head>\n804|<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n805|<script>${readFileSync('vendor/hub/session.js', 'utf8')}</script>\n806|${HUB_METAS}\n807|<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\">\n808|<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\"><title>${TITLE}</title>\n809|<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\n810|</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div>\n811|<script type=\"module\">${safe(readFileSync('.build/bundle.js', 'utf8'))}</script>\n812|</body></html>`;\n813|writeFileSync(OUTPUT_HTML, html);   // OUTPUT_HTML: the deliverable name your brief gives, in root\n814|```\n815|\n816|The session client goes in **unmodified**: the hub replaces an unmodified copy with each new version. Nothing is fetched at runtime, so the game needs no CDN. Bundling doesn't count as editing the engine; `pixel-engine.js` itself stays byte-identical. Output is about 5.4 MB.\n817|\n818|### Browser flags ✔\n819|\n820|**Use all five.** With only the three in the machine notes, `renderer.capture()` failed: `mapAsync ... A valid external Instance reference no longer exists`.\n821|\n822|```\n823|--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader\n824|```\n825|\n826|### Node Playwright and the kit's check ✔\n827|\n828|`npm install playwright@1.63.0` in the dev folder. Then `node check.mjs <page> --keys KeyD*30` works on the built html if it's copied into the dev folder.\n829|\n830|### Screenshots ✔\n831|\n832|The live loop rejects `capture()`, and a WebGPU canvas may screenshot blank. So step first, and composite the HUD:\n833|\n834|```js\n835|const e = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__; e.step(30);          // switches to manual time\n836|const f = await e.renderer.capture();                   // { width, height, pixels }\n837|const c = document.createElement('canvas'); c.width = f.width; c.height = f.height;\n838|const g = c.getContext('2d'); g.putImageData(new ImageData(new Uint8ClampedArray(f.pixels), f.width, f.height), 0, 0);\n839|g.imageSmoothingEnabled = false; if (e.hud.canvas?.width) g.drawImage(e.hud.canvas, 0, 0, f.width, f.height);\n840|return c.toDataURL('image/png');\n841|```\n842|\n843|Put this in `tools/shot.mjs <scene> [--size 1920x1080]`. Use it only for what a script can't judge: composition and legibility. Judge the 10-foot view at 1920×1080.\n844|\n845|### Gamepad stub ✔\n846|\n847|Add as an init script; change the state from the test:\n848|\n849|```js\n850|window.__pad = { buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, () => ({ pressed: false, value: 0, touched: false })), axes: [0, 0, 0, 0] };\n851|navigator.getGamepads = () => [{ id: 'Stub', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: performance.now(), axes: __pad.axes, buttons: __pad.buttons }, null, null, null];\n852|```\n853|\n854|Read inputs through a frame: `moveAxis()` gave (0.8, 0.6) for axes (0.8, -0.6) in-game. Headless, `e.input.setKey('PadCross', true)` works without any stub ✔.\n855|\n856|### Hub harness ✔\n857|\n858|Copy the built html (as `game.html`) with `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` into a temp folder inside the dev folder. Serve it with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` ✔, reading the port from its first output line and stopping it by its PID. An in-process `node:http` server on `127.0.0.1` and port 0 also works, but it must send `Content-Type: text/javascript` for `.js`, or the harness's module imports fail. Then for each of:\n859|\n860|```\n861|harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=1\n862|harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=2\n863|harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5\n864|harness.html?game=game.html&auto=1&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&scenario=host-leave\n865|```\n866|\n867|wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then require `window.__hubCheck.pass`; print failed checks' `name` and `detail`. Each took 10-13 s with a light scene. Keep the card scene light so `ready()` lands inside the 20 s limit even with 4 software-rendered copies. Confirm the served page is yours (its title) before trusting a result. Then open the game outside a session and check it still runs.\n868|\n869|### Headless facts ✔\n870|\n871|- 600 frames with mixers takes about 80 ms, and boot about 240 ms, so full playthroughs are cheap.\n872|- `Engine.headless(game, { camera })`: built-ins load with no asset reader.\n873|- `recording()` and `replay()` reproduce the fingerprint across `loadGame`.\n874|- `input.setPointer(x, y, true)` drives the mouse.\n875|- `ctx.audio` counts plays with no context.\n876|\n877|---\n878|\n879|## 18. Testing\n880|\n881|**One command: `node tools/test.mjs`** prints only failures and one count line (`212/212 passed`). `--fast` runs the Node tests only. Rerun only after changing what a test covers. Prefer scripts to screenshots. Don't use subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit. Keep at most two browsers open.\n882|\n883|**Headless (Node), seconds:**\n884|\n885|1. **Dot:** idle bot < 20% at ring .30; average 35-65%; good > 80%; expert > 95%.\n886|2. **Clips:** `validateClip` empty and `analyzeClip(...).problems` empty for every clip you wrote.\n887|3. **Data:** every model (`checkModel`) and texture (`validateTexture`) clean; all ids resolve; `parseSong` on every song; each song passes the level check in §15; every line fits its box; every character of every string has a glyph.\n888|4. **Every activity:** idle bot finishes with 0★ and no error; expert bot ≥ 2★ (≥ 3★ on easy ones); sloppy < expert; result written; Drips correct.\n889|5. **Full scripted playthrough:** drive the real menus with `setKey` from a fresh save, bots inside activities: new week → all 7 days → every station → goals → unlock schedule → Jar milestones → Long Stand → confession subtracts exactly 7 → credits → Week 2. Assert the state at each step.\n890|6. **Save:** reload mid-week restores; corrupt JSON falls back safely; no storage works.\n891|7. **Pause:** `timeScale` 0, `fixedUpdate` frozen, menu navigable, resume exact.\n892|8. **Dev:** every slider changes live behaviour; reset restores defaults; every tool works.\n893|9. **Attract:** 10 s idle on title and on a menu starts it; no trigger during play; a full loop runs error-free over all items; any input exits.\n894|10. **Determinism:** record an activity, replay it, fingerprints equal.\n895|11. **Medley:** 4 bot lanes, scores in range, windows respected; a ghost lane never simulates.\n896|12. **Voice:** `syllabify` is stable, the same word gives the same syllables, a question rises.\n897|13. **Engine untouched:** `pixel-engine.js` hash equals the kit's.\n898|\n899|**Browser, on the built html via `file://`:**\n900|\n901|14. Boots on WebGPU with no errors; title visible; **music volume is exactly 0.10** on first run.\n902|15. Pad stub: ✕ confirms; prompts show PlayStation glyphs; the Settings option gives Xbox; a key press switches to keycaps; mouse move switches to mouse prompts; hover moves focus; click activates. Record each prompt state in `App.state()` so no picture is needed.\n903|16. Phone profile with touch: message showing, ⚙ present, `engine.touch` null, attract runs.\n904|17. Family Hour with 2 stub pads plus keyboard: three lanes move independently.\n905|18. Audio after a real click: an `AnalyserNode` on the destination reads non-silent for SFX and music; voice in `OfflineAudioContext` has RMS > .02, and Ounce's mean pitch exceeds Coach's.\n906|19. No layout overflow at 1920×1080, 1280×720 and 640×360: widgets record their rects, and the test asserts all fit.\n907|20. WebKit (iPhone profile) and Firefox have no `navigator.gpu` on this machine ✔, so they can only test failure: the engine's \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable\" message shows ✔ and no page error is thrown. Test the touch-only screen itself in Chromium's phone profile, as in test 16.\n908|\n909|**Hub:**\n910|\n911|21. The four harness runs from section 17, all `pass`. Each harness frame is a separate copy of the game, which covers the brief's \"no second player\" note.\n912|22. Outside a session: normal boot with `AIHub.active` false.\n913|\n914|---\n915|\n916|## 19. Build order\n917|\n918|Finish each step with its tests green. Keep the game runnable and the deliverable building from step 1 on.\n919|\n920|1. **Skeleton.** Kit and hub files, build script, test runner, boot scene on `file://`, harness passing with a stub round. Takes minutes, because the recipes above are proven.\n921|2. **The Dot and the kit.** Dot, drivers, actions, device, tunables; font, menu, dialogue, prompts, glyphs; App, scene switching, save; Settings; pause; dev sliders.\n922|3. **One activity, fully.** Holding Still end to end with avatars, Coach, results, voice and music. **Stop and judge the feel here**, since this is the whole game in miniature: check the bot table, then capture a run as frames and confirm the body language reads the Dot.\n923|4. **The island and the week.** Hub, Weigh-In, stations, Report, Jar, schedule, saves. Scripted playthrough started.\n924|5. **Other activities**, in this order: Hoop, Reps, Header, Step, Slackline, Tray, Pier Jump, Jog.\n925|6. **The Medley.** Lanes, Family Hour, session card, ghosts. Harness at full spec.\n926|7. **Attract, Dev tools tab, touch-only, Locker Room, Hall of Numbers.**\n927|8. **The story and the finish.** Ferry, daily beats, Long Stand, confession, ending; line bank to 120+; all songs; every model and particle.\n928|9. **Wrap-up.** About & Credits, exit interview, final tests, one look at each screen at 1920×1080.\n929|\n930|**If you must cut scope,** remove whole activities from the data, in this order: Pier Jump, Vitamin Tray, Island Jog, Overhead Mortgage. Nothing half-built ships, and nothing may look stubbed. **Never cut:** the Dot, Holding Still, Reps, Hoop, Header, Step, Weigh-In, the island, the week, the Long Stand, the Medley, attract, dev mode, Settings, About.\n931|\n932|---\n933|\n934|## 20. Finishing\n935|\n936|**No TODOs, placeholders, stubs or dead menu items.** Every screen works with pad, keyboard and mouse.\n937|\n938|### About & Credits (paged, not dense; L1/R1 or arrows or click)\n939|\n940|Credits; \"This is not medical advice. Ounce is a scale.\"; **Source Information** (every field your brief lists; `unknown` for anything you can't confirm; Usage: `added on import`); **Testing Feedback**; **Engine Feedback**; **Prompt Feedback**; the kit's `CREDITS.md`, shipped as the kit asks: a summary page, then the full text in a scrollable view.\n941|\n942|**Keep one source of truth:** `src/data/about.js` feeds the screen, and `tools/build.mjs` writes the exit-interview file from it, then re-parses it to confirm it is valid JSON. Answer the feedback questions honestly, from your real run, not from this plan.\n943|\n944|For Source Information: Source is Wii Fit; Genre and Perspective as in section 1; Tech: Pixel Engine with its version, three.js r186 and Rapier as bundled in it, esbuild for packaging; Art: the engine's native pixel look; Animation: engine `ClipDef`s with `AnimationMixer`; Audio: engine `Song` and `SoundDef` data plus a Web Audio formant voice; Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, own card, 1-4 players; Family Hour is local. For Research, describe what you did yourself, and note that the director's plan included engine and hub research and spikes.\n945|\n946|### Exit-interview `aiHub` block\n947|\n948|Use the exact shape in your brief. Suggested values:\n949|\n950|- `name`: {TITLE}; `tagline`: yours.\n951|- `type`: `Game`; `genre`: `Sports`; `source`: `Wii Fit`; `series`: `Wii Fit`; `players`: `1–4`.\n952|- `controls`: `Left stick, WASD or mouse: lean. R2, Space or click: breathe. L1/R1, F/J or mouse buttons: step.`\n953|- `tags`: `[\"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"3d\", \"story\"]`.\n954|\n955|### Your final chat reply\n956|\n957|It must contain Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback, as your brief says.\n958|\n959|---\n960|\n961|## 21. Brief coverage checklist\n962|\n963|Tick each before you stop.\n964|\n965|| Brief item | Where |\n966||---|---|\n967|| Genre and perspective chosen | §1, §5, §7 |\n968|| Title: riff on the source's name, picked as the brief says, by you | top of plan, §16 |\n969|| Research: your choice; the director's is here | §4, §17, §20 |\n970|| Single html named as the brief says, in root | §17 |\n971|| Built on the kit; engine unchanged; own systems on top | §16, §17, §18 test 13 |\n972|| Art: engine's look as the base, new assets for the source's feel, library for generic props | §13 |\n973|| Animation: engine's system as the base, new animations | §14 |\n974|| Audio: all in code, gibberish voices, music 10% by default | §15, §18 test 14 |\n975|| Online and multiplayer: hub, and on its own | §12 |\n976|| Dev subfolder, ports, processes, sharing the machine, `file://` first | top of plan, §17, §18 |\n977|| Performance unlimited, no optimisation | §13 |\n978|| Effort is yours to spend; an order and a cut list if you need them | §19 |\n979|| Machine notes: stand-ins for controller, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | §17, §18 |\n980|| Headless tests, scripted playthrough, one command, failures and count only, screenshots only where needed, no review subagents | §18 |\n981|| Original game inspired by the source; world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §2, §8 |\n982|| Feature-complete vertical slice; infrastructure for building out | §3, §5, §16 |\n983|| Dev mode from pause; standard tools; live sliders with reset | §10 |\n984|| Attract: 10 s on title/menus, looping, any input exits, cheats allowed | §11 |\n985|| Writing style like the source's | §8 |\n986|| Controller first at 10 feet; native keyboard and mouse on the same screens | §9 |\n987|| Prompts follow last input; PlayStation glyphs; Xbox option; keys and mouse | §9, §18 test 15 |\n988|| No dense web-style screens | §9 |\n989|| Touch-only: no touch controls, message, settings button, attract runs | §9, §18 test 16 |\n990|| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | §19, §20 |\n991|| Source Information and all feedback in the chat reply and About/Credits | §20 |\n992|| Exit interview in the exact shape, parses as JSON | §20 |","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a1aa23-9552-7210-8d45-f4a3db8beaee"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1aa23-9552-7210-8d45-f4a3db8beaee","task_stream":{"id":"01a1aa23-9552-7210-8d45-f4a3db8beaee","kind":"task"}}}
