{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c63f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa23-73f9-7152-a6b5-3fcdf5d3c2f1"},"sequence":378,"recorded_at":1780531400000751,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","event":{"chunk":"Read text file `Fit Getaway-Wii Fit-muse-wonder-1.0-max-20261104-221652/GUIDE.md`.\n(999 line(s) above)\n1000|\n1001|## 7. Common mistakes\n1002|\n1003|| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n1004|| --- | --- | --- |\n1005|| Blank page, console: CORS / \"Failed to load module script\" | opened with `file://` | serve the folder over HTTP |\n1006|| Console: \"Multiple instances of Three.js being imported\" | three.js loaded twice | use `THREE` from the bundle, nothing else |\n1007|| A red **GAME ERROR** box | an exception in a hook | the box and `engine.errors` have the message, the console the stack: fix the first one |\n1008|| \"Failed to start: ...\" | `setup()` threw (often a bad model path or a typo'd name) | read the message; check the path or the name in API.md |\n1009|| The hero falls through the world | no collider under the mesh | `physics.addStaticBox` for every solid block |\n1010|| The hero is stuck at the start | spawned inside a block | `position` is the feet: put it on the top surface |\n1011|| A trigger never fires | wrong tag, or it doesn't overlap the body | `tag: 'character'` only matches the hero; level geometry needs `includeStatic: true` |\n1012|| A colour is black or a material missing | a colour name that isn't in the palette | the 16 names in section 4 |\n1013|| A model 404s | path not relative to the page | `assets/x.glb` next to `index.html`; built-ins need no file |\n1014|| HUD text shows gaps | characters the 5×7 font doesn't have | uppercase letters, digits, common punctuation |\n1015|| A key does nothing in `fixedUpdate` | `wasPressed` there | `consumePress` in `fixedUpdate`, `wasPressed` in `update` |\n1016|| The ⚙ sits over the HUD's top-right corner on a phone | the settings button (on a mouse it shows only while the pointer moves) | `settings: { button: 'top-left' }`, or `false` and `engine.settings.open()` from your own menu |\n1017|| Side-scroller hero drifts off the lane | `lockDepth` not passed | `lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth` |\n1018|| The camera doesn't follow | `cameraTarget` returns nothing before `setup` ends | return a fallback vector (see the quick start) |\n1019|| Slow, low fps | hundreds of separate meshes | `mergeStaticMeshes` the static level; share materials (`toonMaterial` caches) |\n1020|| Everything is dark | a dimmed sun with no lights | `ctx.lights.request(...)` torches, or raise `ctx.engine.ambient.intensity` |\n1021|| No sound | the browser waits for a key or tap | expected: sound starts on the first input |\n1022|\n1023|## 8. Debugging and checking\n1024|\n1025|The engine is on `window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__` once it runs (also the value `Engine.start` returns).\n1026|A tool waits on `window.__PIXEL_READY__` (it resolves with the engine, or rejects with why the start\n1027|failed); a game puts its own page handles in `ready(ctx)`, which runs then and after each `loadGame`.\n1028|\n1029|```js\n1030|const e = await window.__PIXEL_READY__;   // step() before this throws\n1031|e.state();                // version, backend, fps, camera, look, game status, errors, gpuErrors, ...\n1032|e.errors;                 // exceptions thrown by the game's hooks in the render loop (also on screen)\n1033|e.step(60);               // manual time: exactly 60 frames (1 s), a hook's exception thrown to you; e.manual = false resumes\n1034|                          // step() draws nothing, so a page screenshot still shows the old frame: read the new one with\n1035|                          // await e.renderer.capture() (pixels, no HUD), or set e.manual = false and let a frame draw\n1036|e.input.setKey('KeyD', true); e.step(30); e.input.setKey('KeyD', false);  // play by script\n1037|const rec = e.recording(); const end = e.fingerprint();            // this level's input as JSON, a hash of its state\n1038|await e.replay(rec, () => e.loadGame(new MyGame())); e.fingerprint() === end;  // replayed: the same game\n1039|// Engine.headless(game, { assets }): the same game in Node (below)\n1040|const snap = await e.snapshot(); e.step(300); await e.restore(snap);   // a save-state (Game.snapshot / restore): back at once\n1041|await e.renderer.capture();   // { width, height, pixels }: the exact frame (without the HUD canvas)\n1042|e.game;                   // your game object: e.game.hero.teleport([x, y, z]) to test a spot\n1043|e.setLook(e.lookPresets.noir); e.setCamera({ preset: 'third' }, { syncUrl: false });\n1044|e.audio.counts; e.particles.alive; e.physics.counts(); e.hud.canvas;\n1045|```\n1046|\n1047|URL flags (with `withUrlOptions` in `Engine.start`): `?debug=1` (debug panel),\n1048|`?look=noir`, `?filters=crt,scanlines`,\n1049|`?camera=third`, `?zoom=1.5`, `?mode=raw` (no pixel pass), `?res=320`, `?touch=1`,\n1050|`?quality=low`, `?fps=30`, `?seed=7` (`ctx.random`); they win over the player's saved settings\n1051|(`e.settings.values`). Hotkeys, with `?debug=1`: P pixel/raw, R resolution, \\` debug panel, [ and ]\n1052|cycle looks, M mute.\n1053|\n1054|**`check.mjs` plays a page in a real browser** and fails on anything wrong:\n1055|\n1056|```\n1057|node check.mjs                                  # index.html: start, run 90 frames, screenshot\n1058|node check.mjs --keys KeyD*60,Space*4,KeyD*40   # hold each key for that many frames, in order\n1059|node check.mjs examples/side-scroller.html --cameras --looks noir,handheld\n1060|node check.mjs \"index.html?look=handheld&zoom=1.5\"   # with URL flags\n1061|node check.mjs --sheets models.js               # sheets of your own models and textures (ASSETS.md)\n1062|```\n1063|\n1064|It plays on WebGPU in Chromium's headless shell, so it needs no display. It writes\n1065|`check/<page>.png` (the frame with the HUD), the camera and look shots and\n1066|`check/report.json` (errors, warnings, `state()`), and prints a summary: the backend, frames\n1067|and your `status()`. Exit code 0: the game started, ran with no page, console, game or GPU\n1068|errors and drew a real picture; 1: it didn't; 2: the tool couldn't run (a browser without\n1069|WebGPU, bad arguments, no page, no browser; `--help` lists the options). It needs Node 20.15+ (or 22.2+) and Playwright\n1070|(`npm i -D playwright && npx playwright install chromium`; a global install works too), or\n1071|`playwright-core` plus a Chromium in `CHROMIUM_PATH`. **Look at the PNGs**: a passing check only proves nothing crashed.\n1072|\n1073|**Play it in Node.** `Engine.headless(game, { assets })` runs a game as `Engine.start` does, minus\n1074|the GPU and DOM, on manual time, from the kit alone; `assets` reads the game's files.\n1075|`node check.mjs --headless game.js` plays its `createGame()` (the starter's) for the `--keys`,\n1076|replays it in a fresh game and fails on an error or a replay that ends elsewhere. By hand:\n1077|\n1078|```js\n1079|// test.mjs, beside game.js\n1080|import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\n1081|import { Engine } from './pixel-engine.js';\n1082|import { createGame } from './game.js';\n1083|\n1084|const assets = async (path) => new Uint8Array(await readFile(new URL(path, import.meta.url))).buffer;\n1085|const engine = await Engine.headless(createGame(), { assets });\n1086|engine.step(60); // input.setKey to play; a hook's error throws\n1087|const end = engine.fingerprint();\n1088|await engine.replay(engine.recording(), () => engine.loadGame(createGame()));\n1089|console.log(engine.state().status, engine.fingerprint() === end);\n1090|```\n1091|\n1092|Code that touches `document` guards it, as the starter does.\n1093|\n1094|## 9. Before you hand back\n1095|\n1096|- [ ] `node check.mjs` exits 0 for every page, with `--keys` that actually play the game\n1097|      (reach a goal, collect something, lose a life).\n1098|- [ ] `node check.mjs --headless game.js` exits 0 with the same `--keys`.\n1099|- [ ] You looked at the screenshots: the scene reads, the HUD is legible, nothing is black or\n1100|      clipped, the hero is on the ground.\n1101|- [ ] `status()` reports the game's state, and it changes as you play.\n1102|- [ ] No WebGL-era APIs, no second three.js, no `new PointLight`, no unknown palette names.\n1103|- [ ] The controls are written down (the header comment of `game.js`, or on screen).\n1104|- [ ] On a phone (or `?touch=1`) the game is playable with the touch buttons, or you set\n1105|      `touchButtons` for its own actions.\n1106|\n1107|## 10. Versions\n1108|\n1109|`ENGINE_VERSION` (also `Engine.version` and `state().version`) is the engine's version, and\n1110|the kit's `CHANGELOG.md` says what changed in each. To upgrade a game, replace\n1111|`pixel-engine.js` (and `pixel-engine.d.ts`, `types/` if you use them), read the changelog\n1112|entries since the old version, then run `node check.mjs` again. The newest release of the kit is\n1113|at the URL in `manifest.json`'s `latest`, and every release (from 0.39.0, its changelog as the\n1114|notes) stays downloadable from `releases`. The kit's `README.md` says how to build\n1115|it from the engine's repository (`source`) instead.","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a1aa24-18a8-7bc2-8307-dcfa7f0daa3d"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1aa24-18a8-7bc2-8307-dcfa7f0daa3d","task_stream":{"id":"01a1aa24-18a8-7bc2-8307-dcfa7f0daa3d","kind":"task"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c641","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa23-73f9-7152-a6b5-3fcdf5d3c2f1"},"sequence":379,"recorded_at":1780531400000753,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a1aa24-18a8-7bc2-8307-dcfa7f0daa3d"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1aa24-18a8-7bc2-8307-dcfa7f0daa3d","task_stream":{"id":"01a1aa24-18a8-7bc2-8307-dcfa7f0daa3d","kind":"task"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c643","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa23-73f9-7152-a6b5-3fcdf5d3c2f1"},"sequence":380,"recorded_at":1780531400000755,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"call_id":"call_01a1aa24146173d9989169599d283ce8","command_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","correlation_facts":{"outcome":"success","tool_name":"read_file"},"kind":"tool_result","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","kind":"run"},"text":"Read text file `Fit Getaway-Wii Fit-muse-wonder-1.0-max-20261104-221652/game.js`.\n1|// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\n2|import { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\n3|\n4|const { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\n5|\n6|/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\n7|function block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\n8|  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\n9|  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\n10|  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\n11|  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\n12|  return mesh;\n13|}\n14|\n15|class CoinGarden {\n16|  name = 'Coin Garden';\n17|  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\n18|  coins = [];\n19|  collected = 0;\n20|  won = false;\n21|  target = new Vector3();\n22|  ground = new Vector3();\n23|\n24|  async setup(ctx) {\n25|    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\n26|    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\n27|    scene.add(\n28|      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\n29|        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\n30|        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\n31|        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\n32|        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\n33|      ]),\n34|    );\n35|    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\n36|    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\n37|    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\n38|      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\n39|      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\n40|      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\n41|      scene.add(mesh);\n42|      const item = { mesh, taken: false };\n43|      physics.trigger({ cylinder: { halfHeight: 0.6, radius: 0.5 } }, [x, y, z], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.collect(ctx, item) });\n44|      this.coins.push(item);\n45|    }\n46|    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\n47|    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\n48|    this.model = hero.scene;\n49|    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\n50|    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\n51|    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\n52|    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 4], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\n53|    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\n54|  }\n55|\n56|  collect(ctx, item) {\n57|    item.taken = true;\n58|    item.mesh.visible = false;\n59|    this.collected++;\n60|    ctx.audio.play('coin');\n61|    ctx.particles.burst('sparkle', item.mesh.position);\n62|  }\n63|\n64|  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\n65|    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input); // filled in place after the first step\n66|    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input); // movement and forces: fixed 60 Hz step\n67|  }\n68|\n69|  update(ctx, dt) {\n70|    this.hero.updateVisual(this.model, dt, ctx.physics.alpha); // pose and interpolate\n71|    const feet = this.model.position;\n72|    const ground = ctx.physics.groundBelow(this.ground.set(feet.x, feet.y + 0.1, feet.z), 20, this.hero.body);\n73|    if (ground) this.shadow.place(feet.x, ground.y, feet.z, feet.y - ground.y);\n74|    for (const c of this.coins) if (!c.taken) c.mesh.rotation.y += dt * 3;\n75|    if (!this.won && this.collected === this.coins.length) {\n76|      this.won = true;\n77|      this.hero.celebrate();\n78|      ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\n79|    }\n80|    ctx.hud.clear();\n81|    ctx.hud.text(6, 6, `COINS ${this.collected}/${this.coins.length}`, { color: 'sand' });\n82|    if (this.won) ctx.hud.text(0, 0, 'YOU WIN!', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2, shadow: 'navy' });\n83|  }\n84|\n85|  cameraTarget() {\n86|    const p = this.model?.position ?? this.target.set(0, 0, 4);\n87|    return this.target.set(p.x, p.y + 0.9, p.z);\n88|  }\n89|\n90|  onCameraChange(ctx) {\n91|    this.hero.setLockDepth(ctx.camera.lockDepth); // side view: stay on the lane\n92|    this.model.visible = !ctx.camera.hidesTarget; // first person: no body in the way\n93|  }\n94|\n95|  status() {\n96|    return `coins ${this.collected}/${this.coins.length}`;\n97|  }\n98|}\n99|\n100|/** A fresh game: the page starts one, and `node check.mjs --headless` plays one in Node (section 8). */\n101|export const createGame = () => new CoinGarden();\n102|\n103|if (typeof document !== 'undefined') await Engine.start(createGame(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso' } }));"}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c645","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa23-73f9-7152-a6b5-3fcdf5d3c2f1"},"sequence":381,"recorded_at":1780531400000757,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"call_id":"call_01a1aa2414ef74a78693d91b5073a19e","command_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","correlation_facts":{"outcome":"success","tool_name":"read_file"},"kind":"tool_result","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","kind":"run"},"text":"Read text file `Fit Getaway-Wii Fit-muse-wonder-1.0-max-20261104-221652/index.html`.\n1|<!doctype html>\n2|<html lang=\"en\">\n3|  <head>\n4|    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n5|    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\" />\n6|    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n7|    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\n8|    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\n9|  </head>\n10|  <body>\n11|    <div id=\"app\"></div>\n12|    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./game.js\"></script>\n13|  </body>\n14|</html>"}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c647","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa23-73f9-7152-a6b5-3fcdf5d3c2f1"},"sequence":382,"recorded_at":1780531400000759,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"call_id":"call_01a1aa24156776d29d010e9781fafd93","command_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","correlation_facts":{"outcome":"success","tool_name":"read_file"},"kind":"tool_result","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","kind":"run"},"text":"Read text file `Fit Getaway-Wii Fit-muse-wonder-1.0-max-20261104-221652/GUIDE.md`.\n(999 line(s) above)\n1000|\n1001|## 7. Common mistakes\n1002|\n1003|| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n1004|| --- | --- | --- |\n1005|| Blank page, console: CORS / \"Failed to load module script\" | opened with `file://` | serve the folder over HTTP |\n1006|| Console: \"Multiple instances of Three.js being imported\" | three.js loaded twice | use `THREE` from the bundle, nothing else |\n1007|| A red **GAME ERROR** box | an exception in a hook | the box and `engine.errors` have the message, the console the stack: fix the first one |\n1008|| \"Failed to start: ...\" | `setup()` threw (often a bad model path or a typo'd name) | read the message; check the path or the name in API.md |\n1009|| The hero falls through the world | no collider under the mesh | `physics.addStaticBox` for every solid block |\n1010|| The hero is stuck at the start | spawned inside a block | `position` is the feet: put it on the top surface |\n1011|| A trigger never fires | wrong tag, or it doesn't overlap the body | `tag: 'character'` only matches the hero; level geometry needs `includeStatic: true` |\n1012|| A colour is black or a material missing | a colour name that isn't in the palette | the 16 names in section 4 |\n1013|| A model 404s | path not relative to the page | `assets/x.glb` next to `index.html`; built-ins need no file |\n1014|| HUD text shows gaps | characters the 5×7 font doesn't have | uppercase letters, digits, common punctuation |\n1015|| A key does nothing in `fixedUpdate` | `wasPressed` there | `consumePress` in `fixedUpdate`, `wasPressed` in `update` |\n1016|| The ⚙ sits over the HUD's top-right corner on a phone | the settings button (on a mouse it shows only while the pointer moves) | `settings: { button: 'top-left' }`, or `false` and `engine.settings.open()` from your own menu |\n1017|| Side-scroller hero drifts off the lane | `lockDepth` not passed | `lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth` |\n1018|| The camera doesn't follow | `cameraTarget` returns nothing before `setup` ends | return a fallback vector (see the quick start) |\n1019|| Slow, low fps | hundreds of separate meshes | `mergeStaticMeshes` the static level; share materials (`toonMaterial` caches) |\n1020|| Everything is dark | a dimmed sun with no lights | `ctx.lights.request(...)` torches, or raise `ctx.engine.ambient.intensity` |\n1021|| No sound | the browser waits for a key or tap | expected: sound starts on the first input |\n1022|\n1023|## 8. Debugging and checking\n1024|\n1025|The engine is on `window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__` once it runs (also the value `Engine.start` returns).\n1026|A tool waits on `window.__PIXEL_READY__` (it resolves with the engine, or rejects with why the start\n1027|failed); a game puts its own page handles in `ready(ctx)`, which runs then and after each `loadGame`.\n1028|\n1029|```js\n1030|const e = await window.__PIXEL_READY__;   // step() before this throws\n1031|e.state();                // version, backend, fps, camera, look, game status, errors, gpuErrors, ...\n1032|e.errors;                 // exceptions thrown by the game's hooks in the render loop (also on screen)\n1033|e.step(60);               // manual time: exactly 60 frames (1 s), a hook's exception thrown to you; e.manual = false resumes\n1034|                          // step() draws nothing, so a page screenshot still shows the old frame: read the new one with\n1035|                          // await e.renderer.capture() (pixels, no HUD), or set e.manual = false and let a frame draw\n1036|e.input.setKey('KeyD', true); e.step(30); e.input.setKey('KeyD', false);  // play by script\n1037|const rec = e.recording(); const end = e.fingerprint();            // this level's input as JSON, a hash of its state\n1038|await e.replay(rec, () => e.loadGame(new MyGame())); e.fingerprint() === end;  // replayed: the same game\n1039|// Engine.headless(game, { assets }): the same game in Node (below)\n1040|const snap = await e.snapshot(); e.step(300); await e.restore(snap);   // a save-state (Game.snapshot / restore): back at once\n1041|await e.renderer.capture();   // { width, height, pixels }: the exact frame (without the HUD canvas)\n1042|e.game;                   // your game object: e.game.hero.teleport([x, y, z]) to test a spot\n1043|e.setLook(e.lookPresets.noir); e.setCamera({ preset: 'third' }, { syncUrl: false });\n1044|e.audio.counts; e.particles.alive; e.physics.counts(); e.hud.canvas;\n1045|```\n1046|\n1047|URL flags (with `withUrlOptions` in `Engine.start`): `?debug=1` (debug panel),\n1048|`?look=noir`, `?filters=crt,scanlines`,\n1049|`?camera=third`, `?zoom=1.5`, `?mode=raw` (no pixel pass), `?res=320`, `?touch=1`,\n1050|`?quality=low`, `?fps=30`, `?seed=7` (`ctx.random`); they win over the player's saved settings\n1051|(`e.settings.values`). Hotkeys, with `?debug=1`: P pixel/raw, R resolution, \\` debug panel, [ and ]\n1052|cycle looks, M mute.\n1053|\n1054|**`check.mjs` plays a page in a real browser** and fails on anything wrong:\n1055|\n1056|```\n1057|node check.mjs                                  # index.html: start, run 90 frames, screenshot\n1058|node check.mjs --keys KeyD*60,Space*4,KeyD*40   # hold each key for that many frames, in order\n1059|node check.mjs examples/side-scroller.html --cameras --looks noir,handheld\n1060|node check.mjs \"index.html?look=handheld&zoom=1.5\"   # with URL flags\n1061|node check.mjs --sheets models.js               # sheets of your own models and textures (ASSETS.md)\n1062|```\n1063|\n1064|It plays on WebGPU in Chromium's headless shell, so it needs no display. It writes\n1065|`check/<page>.png` (the frame with the HUD), the camera and look shots and\n1066|`check/report.json` (errors, warnings, `state()`), and prints a summary: the backend, frames\n1067|and your `status()`. Exit code 0: the game started, ran with no page, console, game or GPU\n1068|errors and drew a real picture; 1: it didn't; 2: the tool couldn't run (a browser without\n1069|WebGPU, bad arguments, no page, no browser; `--help` lists the options). It needs Node 20.15+ (or 22.2+) and Playwright\n1070|(`npm i -D playwright && npx playwright install chromium`; a global install works too), or\n1071|`playwright-core` plus a Chromium in `CHROMIUM_PATH`. **Look at the PNGs**: a passing check only proves nothing crashed.\n1072|\n1073|**Play it in Node.** `Engine.headless(game, { assets })` runs a game as `Engine.start` does, minus\n1074|the GPU and DOM, on manual time, from the kit alone; `assets` reads the game's files.\n1075|`node check.mjs --headless game.js` plays its `createGame()` (the starter's) for the `--keys`,\n1076|replays it in a fresh game and fails on an error or a replay that ends elsewhere. By hand:\n1077|\n1078|```js\n1079|// test.mjs, beside game.js\n1080|import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';\n1081|import { Engine } from './pixel-engine.js';\n1082|import { createGame } from './game.js';\n1083|\n1084|const assets = async (path) => new Uint8Array(await readFile(new URL(path, import.meta.url))).buffer;\n1085|const engine = await Engine.headless(createGame(), { assets });\n1086|engine.step(60); // input.setKey to play; a hook's error throws\n1087|const end = engine.fingerprint();\n1088|await engine.replay(engine.recording(), () => engine.loadGame(createGame()));\n1089|console.log(engine.state().status, engine.fingerprint() === end);\n1090|```\n1091|\n1092|Code that touches `document` guards it, as the starter does.\n1093|\n1094|## 9. Before you hand back\n1095|\n1096|- [ ] `node check.mjs` exits 0 for every page, with `--keys` that actually play the game\n1097|      (reach a goal, collect something, lose a life).\n1098|- [ ] `node check.mjs --headless game.js` exits 0 with the same `--keys`.\n1099|- [ ] You looked at the screenshots: the scene reads, the HUD is legible, nothing is black or\n1100|      clipped, the hero is on the ground.\n1101|- [ ] `status()` reports the game's state, and it changes as you play.\n1102|- [ ] No WebGL-era APIs, no second three.js, no `new PointLight`, no unknown palette names.\n1103|- [ ] The controls are written down (the header comment of `game.js`, or on screen).\n1104|- [ ] On a phone (or `?touch=1`) the game is playable with the touch buttons, or you set\n1105|      `touchButtons` for its own actions.\n1106|\n1107|## 10. Versions\n1108|\n1109|`ENGINE_VERSION` (also `Engine.version` and `state().version`) is the engine's version, and\n1110|the kit's `CHANGELOG.md` says what changed in each. To upgrade a game, replace\n1111|`pixel-engine.js` (and `pixel-engine.d.ts`, `types/` if you use them), read the changelog\n1112|entries since the old version, then run `node check.mjs` again. The newest release of the kit is\n1113|at the URL in `manifest.json`'s `latest`, and every release (from 0.39.0, its changelog as the\n1114|notes) stays downloadable from `releases`. The kit's `README.md` says how to build\n1115|it from the engine's repository (`source`) instead."}}
