{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c675","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa23-73f9-7152-a6b5-3fcdf5d3c2f1"},"sequence":405,"recorded_at":1780531400000805,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","event":{"chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-5-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cd \\\"Fit Getaway-Wii Fit-muse-wonder-1.0-max-20261104-221652\\\"\\ngrep -n \\\"setVolume\\\\|playMusic\\\\|register\\\\|Song\\\\|parseSong\\\" API.md | head -n 60\\necho ---\\ngrep -n \\\"class Engine\\\\|Engine.start\\\\|headless\\\\|loadGame\\\\|timeScale\\\\|setCamera\\\" API.md | head -n 60\\necho ---\\ngrep -n \\\"moveAxis\\\\|gamepadButtons\\\\|setKey\\\\|pointer\\\" API.md | head -n 60\\necho ---\\ngrep -n \\\"validateClip\\\\|analyzeClip\\\\|compileClips\\\\|HERO_CLIPS\\\\|placeFeet\\\\|gaitClip\\\\|mirror\\\" API.md | head -n 60\\necho ---\\ngrep -n \\\"checkModel\\\\|buildModel\\\\|textureDef\\\\|model(\\\" API.md | head -n 40\",\n  \"description\": \"Search engine API signatures\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"14:8. Audio: `attenuation`, `AudioManager`, `AudioSettings`, `Instrument`, `Listener`, `muffleCutoff`, `noteFrequency`, `parseSong`, `PLAYGROUND_SONG`, `PlayOptions`, `renderSound`, `SFX`, `SfxName`, `Song`, `SoundDef`, `Spatial`, `spatialize`, `SpatialOptions`, `Voice`, `VoiceSettings`, `VolumeChannel`, `Wave`\\n2465:sequencer (`Song`, data), optional audio files, and master / sfx / music volume + mute\\n2475:- `readonly sounds: Map<string, SoundDef>`: Sound registry: the built-in SFX plus anything registered or loaded.\\n2484:- `register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void`: Add or replace a sound effect (data, see SoundDef).\\n2485:- `play(sound: string | SoundDef, options: PlayOptions = {}): boolean`: Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\\n2490:- `playMusic(song: Song | null, name = 'song'): void`: Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music.\\n2493:- `setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void`\\n2496:- `resetVolumes(): void`: The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset).\\n2536:### parseSong()\\n2539:function parseSong(song: Song): ParsedSong\\n2547:const PLAYGROUND_SONG: Song\\n2572:Built-in retro sound effects, as data. Tweak numbers here (or register your own with\\n2573:`ctx.audio.register(name, def)`) and every `ctx.audio.play(name)` picks them up.\\n2582:### interface Song\\n2740:- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\\n2742:- `register(name: string, preset: ParticlePreset): void`: Add or replace a named preset. Replacing frees the old preset's emitter.\\n2758:`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\\n---\\n132:### class Engine\\n136:- `static headless(game: Game, options: HeadlessOptions = {}): Promise<Engine>`: The engine without a page (docs/engine/headless.md): the same boot, game code and frames as `start`, with a `HeadlessView` that draws nothing, in Node. No DOM, no GPU, no listeners, no AudioContext (`audio.counts` still counts), no panels; errors go to `engin…\\n160:- `get gpu: PixelRenderer | null`: The page's renderer, for direct GPU work (readbacks, the canvas, compute): null headless (`Engine.headless`), where nothing is drawn. Gameplay reads `renderer`, which both have.\\n161:- `get game: Game`: The running game. Replace it with `loadGame()`.\\n164:- `get timeScale: number`: Game speed: 1 normal, 0.25 slow motion, 2 double, 0 frozen (a menu: key presses made meanwhile are dropped, like a pause). Scales game time, physics, animation, particles, tweens and the camera follow; not transitions, shake or the render loop. Back to 1 when…\\n175:- `setCamera(config: CameraConfig, options: { syncUrl?: boolean } = {}): CameraRig`: Swap the camera preset mid-game (review tool: presets are a per-game choice). The player, physics and the rest of the world are left exactly as they are. `free` and `fixed` without an explicit position start from the view currently on screen. Keeps `?camera=`…\\n185:- `state(): { version: string; game: string; seed: number; ready: boolean; paused: boolean; time: number; timeScale: number; hitstop: number; screen: ScreenFxState; backend: BackendName; ... 19 more ...; status: string; }`: Snapshot for tests, tooling and agents.\\n187:- `loadGame(game: Game, options: { camera?: CameraConfig } = {}): Promise<void>`: Unload the running game and start `game` in the same engine (renderer, canvas, camera rig, input, audio context and debug UI stay).\\n188:- `dispose(): void`: Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM, GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\\n192:- `replay(rec: Recording, start: () => unknown, o: { frames?: number } = {}): Promise<void>`: Play a recording back: its seed and start time are restored, `start` loads the level it was made in (e.g. `() => engine.loadGame(new MyGame())`; it must not wait on frames, so load without a transition), then every frame runs with the recorded input, in manua…\\n276:- `ready?(ctx: GameContext): void`: Runs when the engine starts running this game: after `Engine.start` (just before `__PIXEL_READY__` resolves) and after each `loadGame`. Install page handles for tools here (`window.__MYGAME__`), so they never exist before the engine can step. An exception is…\\n285:- `onCameraChange?(ctx: GameContext): void`: Called after `engine.setCamera()` swapped the camera preset mid-game. The world, physics and player are untouched; adjust anything that depends on the preset (e.g. side-scroller lane lock, hiding the player model in first person).\\n286:- `dispose?(ctx: GameContext): void`: Called when the game is unloaded (`engine.loadGame(other)` or `engine.dispose()`), before the engine removes its scene objects, physics bodies, triggers, particles, HUD and music. Free anything else the game owns: DOM, timers, listeners, HMR hooks.\\n307:`Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs.\\n538:`Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ container, camera: { preset: 'side', zoom: 1.2 } }))`.\\n573:reviewing, `engine.setCamera()` swaps presets live without touching the world. `free`\\n707:type BackendName = 'WebGPU' | 'headless'\\n710:The engine renders with WebGPU only (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 6); `headless` draws nothing (`Engine.headless`).\\n1065:- `readonly container: HTMLElement`: The page element the canvas sits in; null headless.\\n1092:- `setCamera(camera: Camera): void`: Point both passes at a different camera (camera preset hot-swap). The pipeline, canvas and all nodes stay the same; only the camera the scene is rendered with changes.\\n2470:(headless tests, old browsers), every call is a silent no-op that still records what\\n2639:- `readonly settings: Readonly<Required<VoiceSettings>>`: The values last set (kept headless too, so games and tests can read them).\\n2856:`public/` in Node, and `Engine.headless` installs the one it is given. Files a build embeds\\n3899:The Rapier 3D physics module (`@dimforge/rapier3d` 0.20), already initialised by `Engine.start`. Most games only need `ctx.physics`; use `RAPIER.X` for raw shapes, joints and queries on `ctx.physics.world`.\\n4186:pads. Game time (they pause, slow down and freeze with `engine.timeScale` and hitstops)\\n4351:The viewport a headless view frames by default: the riftlight-replay page's (Riftlight's `fill` gives 480×270).\\n4356:- `readonly container: null`: The page element the canvas sits in; null headless.\\n4359:- `readonly recoveries: 0`: How many times a lost GPU device was recovered from (0 headless).\\n4384:- `setCamera(camera: Camera): void`\\n4389:- `capture(): Promise<CapturedFrame>`: The frame as pixels; rejects headless.\\n4617:- `readonly view?: Viewport`: The viewport it was recorded on, as it was when the level began (CSS pixels and DPR): the art resolution, pointer aim and the HUD's layout follow it. A headless replay frames for it; a page warns when its own differs. A page resized during the level is not fo…\\n4965:  await engine.loadGame(next);\\n5037:- `readonly container: HTMLElement | null`: The page element the canvas sits in; null headless.\\n5040:- `readonly recoveries: number`: How many times a lost GPU device was recovered from (0 headless).\\n5063:- `setCamera(camera: Camera): void`\\n5069:- `capture(): Promise<CapturedFrame>`: The frame as pixels; rejects headless.\\n---\\n220:- `settings?: { button?: TouchCorner | boolean; key?: string | false }`: The player's settings (`engine.settings`): look, pixel art, pixel size, quality, frame rate, sound and debug info, in a panel the ⚙ button opens. `button`: its corner (default, or true: 'top-right'; on a mouse it shows while the pointer moves), or false for n…\\n221:- `touch?: boolean`: On-screen joystick + buttons. Default: auto (coarse pointer), or ?touch=1 / ?touch=0.\\n594:- `rayAt(x: number, y: number, origin: Vector3, dir: Vector3): void`: The ray through screen point (x, y) in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up, as `input.pointer` gives them): where it starts (on the near plane) and its unit direction. For picking things with the mouse, or aiming at it. An orthographic rig stands far b…\\n625:Eyes of the character: mouse look (click to lock the pointer) or Q/E to turn. No zoom.\\n2253:A pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\\n2275:KEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \\\"standard\\\" layout:\\n2289:Keyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\\n2292:- Gamepads (standard mapping): the left stick feeds `moveAxis()` (radial deadzone), the\\n2293:  right stick feeds the pointer delta (camera look), buttons press key codes\\n2294:  (`gamepadButtons`). Polled once per frame by the engine (`beginFrame`).\\n2295:- Pointer: accumulated movement per frame (while a button is held or the pointer is\\n2296:  locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n2303:- `readonly mouseDelta: { x: number; y: number; }`: Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock).\\n2304:- `readonly pointer: { x: number; y: number; over: boolean; touch: boolean; }`: Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up: `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now. Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n2306:- `wantsPointerLock: boolean`: When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera).\\n2311:- `gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>`: Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS).\\n2313:- `gamepadLookSpeed: number`: Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt.\\n2315:- `get playing: boolean`: True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events, `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send` are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n2317:- `attachPointer(el: HTMLElement): void`: Listen for pointer input on the game canvas. Only pointers that went down on the canvas drive the camera (so a touch joystick doesn't orbit it). Two canvas touches pinch to zoom (emitted as wheel ticks).\\n2319:- `release(): void`: Let go of everything held (keys, gamepad buttons, sticks, pointer buttons); queued presses stay.\\n2320:- `reset(): void`: Forget held keys, presses, sticks and pointer movement (e.g. when a level loads).\\n2322:- `get pointerLocked: boolean`\\n2328:- `state(): InputState`: Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames.\\n2332:- `moveAxis(): { x: number; y: number }`: -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\\n2334:- `setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void`: Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false).\\n2335:- `setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void`: Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not.\\n2338:- `get buttonEvents: readonly ButtonEvent[]`: This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play read…\\n2342:- `addPointer(dx: number, dy: number, wheel = 0): void`: Test hook: inject pointer movement / wheel for the next frame.\\n2343:- `snapshot(dt: number, last?: SnapshotMemory): InputFrame`: This frame's input as data (after `beginFrame`), for a recording. `last` is the frame before: unchanged held keys, pointer and gamepad connection are left out.\\n2345:- `playAfter(f: InputFrame): void`: Replay, after `beginFrame` (which polled no gamepads): sticks, pointer, wheel, gamepad connection.\\n2350:Optional fields are left out when empty or zero; `held` and `pointer` also when unchanged\\n2360:- `pointer?: [number, number, number, number]`: Pointer position (normalised device coordinates), over the canvas (1/0), buttons (`mouseButtons`: what `held` says).\\n2362:- `touch?: boolean`: Whether the pointer is a touch (`pointer.touch`), when that changes.\\n2363:- `clicks?: [string, 0 | 1, number, number][]`: Pointer buttons pressed (1) and let go (0) this frame, in order, each where the pointer was (`buttonEvents`).\\n2369:What input a later frame still reads, as data (`engine.snapshot()`): keys held, presses not yet used and how old they are, the pointer.\\n2373:- `readonly pointer: readonly [number, number, number, number]`\\n2430:Shown automatically on coarse pointers, or with `?touch=1`.\\n2469:first key / pointer / touch input. Before that, and wherever Web Audio does not exist\\n4617:- `readonly view?: Viewport`: The viewport it was recorded on, as it was when the level began (CSS pixels and DPR): the art resolution, pointer aim and the HUD's layout follow it. A headless replay frames for it; a page warns when its own differs. A page resized during the level is not fo…\\n---\\n18:12. Animation toolkit: `analyzeClip`, `ClipDef`, `ClipReport`, `compileClip`, `compileClips`, `Foot`, `FootGoal`, `gaitClip`, `gaitPartners`, `GaitSpec`, `Key`, `LegDef`, `LegStepper`, `LegStepperOptions`, `mirror`, `placeFeet`, `Pose`, `renderCurves`, `renderSheet`, `RigSpec`, `sampleClip`, `SheetImage`, `SpringChain`, `SpringChainOptions`, `Squash`, `twoBoneIK`, `validateClip`\\n19:13. Hero kit: `HERO_CLIPS`, `HERO_MODEL`, `HERO_RAGDOLL`, `HERO_RIG`\\n1071:- `lookVersion: number`: Counts look changes (UIs that mirror the look re-sync when it moves).\\n1091:- `get activeCamera: Camera`: The camera the frame is drawn from (mirrors reflect it).\\n3541:### analyzeClip()\\n3544:function analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\\n3556:- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\\n3597:### compileClips()\\n3600:function compileClips(defs: readonly ClipDef[], rig: RigSpec, model: Object3D): AnimationClip[]\\n3616:  placeFeet({ Pelvis: { p: [0, -0.2, 0] }, Torso: [20, 0, 0] }, rig, {\\n3634:### gaitClip()\\n3637:function gaitClip(rig: RigSpec, g: GaitSpec): ClipDef\\n3725:### mirror()\\n3728:function mirror(pose: Pose, rig: Pick<RigSpec, 'mirror'>): Pose\\n3731:Mirror a pose left ↔ right (rig.mirror pairs; Y/Z rotations and X offsets flip).\\n3733:### placeFeet()\\n3736:function placeFeet(pose: Pose, rig: RigSpec, goals: Partial<Record<Side, FootGoal>>): Pose\\n3770:- `mirror: Readonly<Record<string, string>>`: Left/right counterparts for mirroring.\\n3844:### validateClip()\\n3847:function validateClip(clip: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec): string[]\\n3854:### HERO_CLIPS\\n3857:const HERO_CLIPS: readonly ClipDef[]\\n4360:- `lookVersion: number`: Counts look changes (UIs that mirror the look re-sync when it moves).\\n4687:The layer for screens and mirrors: drawn by the main camera, never by a RenderView.\\n4786:- `put(i: number, x: number, y: number, z: number, frame?: number, flip?: boolean): void`: `set` without the options object, for many sprites every frame: position, then frame and mirror.\\n5041:- `readonly lookVersion: number`: Counts look changes (UIs that mirror the look re-sync when it moves).\\n---\\n17:11. Models and textures (ASSETS.md): `addModelColliders`, `around`, `assetProgress`, `AssetReader`, `BakedTexture`, `bakeTexture`, `boxFrame`, `buildModel`, `Catalog`, `CatalogEntry`, `checkModel`, `decodePng`, `DEFAULT_TEXEL`, `ExpandedModel`, `expandModel`, `gridOf`, `groupVariants`, `hudSprite`, `ImportError`, `importSheet`, `LICENCES`, `loadModel`, `loadPack`, `loadPackIndex`, `meanColour`, `model`, `Model`, `MODEL_FAMILIES`, `MODEL_LIBRARY`, `ModelBinding`, `ModelBuild`, `ModelCatalog`, `ModelCheck`, `ModelCollider`, `ModelDef`, `ModelError`, `ModelLight`, `ModelLightRequest`, `ModelOptions`, `ModelPack`, `ModelPart`, `ModelProvenance`, `modelSheet`, `ModelSheet`, `ModelSheetOptions`, `MOVING_TEXEL`, `PackIndex`, `PackIndexEntry`, `packTextures`, `parsePack`, `PngError`, `preloadModels`, `RgbaImage`, `rowOf`, `scatterOf`, `searchDefs`, `SearchHit`, `searchHits`, `SearchOptions`, `searchWords`, `setAssetReader`, `SheetImport`, `SheetImportOptions`, `spriteSheet`, `TEXTURE_FAMILIES`, `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`, `TextureCatalog`, `TextureCheck`, `textureDef`, `TextureDef`, `TextureError`, `TextureLayer`, `textureMap`, `textureSheet`, `TextureSheet`, `TextureSheetOptions`, `validateModel`, `validateTexture`, `VariantGroup`, `variantName`\\n2884:### buildModel()\\n2887:function buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\\n2909:### checkModel()\\n2912:function checkModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: CheckOptions = {}): ModelCheck\\n3033:pack's ModelDefs, to build from with `buildModel(id, { catalog })`; `into` also adds them to a\\n3055:### model()\\n3058:function model(def: T): T\\n3107:and `buildModel('id')` resolve ids through one (the library unless a build passes another);\\n3213:palette and `checkModel`'s problems and warnings over every param's range. Software-drawn: no\\n3231:`modelSheet`'s options: `buildModel`'s (`params`, `seed`, `palette`, `light`, `catalog` where\\n3437:### textureDef()\\n3440:function textureDef(def: T): T\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 17605,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 4402,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a1aa24-2b0a-74d3-8b3f-5bae93a12cd7"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa23-76a1-7912-8c1f-0bbd20af817a","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1aa24-2b0a-74d3-8b3f-5bae93a12cd7","task_stream":{"id":"01a1aa24-2b0a-74d3-8b3f-5bae93a12cd7","kind":"task"}}}
